{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name","id":1496192,"title":"Shadow Name too close to your real name","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-04T07:10:45-07:00","id":1496192,"title":"Shadow Name too close to your real name","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I would like to know the implications of my shadow name sounding too close to my real name. My character <b>Edward </b>(Acanthus, Free Council), has been looking into the symbolism of Air, Water and not following the current... So he wants to be <b>Eddy</b>, problem is that is too close to his real name or to the diminutive <b>Eddie</b>.<br /> <br /> What are the implications of having shadow and real names too close? Sympathetic effects and resonances included.<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T12:02:41-07:00","id":1496212,"title":"","content":"I think he would only run into issues if he lets his mortal friends call him Eddy, which would lead to him being &quot;that guy&quot; who INSISTS on being called Ed or Edward and corrects people every time they said Eddy. I'd also have him try to keep other mages/monsters from knowing his real name.<br /> <br /> Any sleeper who has accepted Eddy as a name for Edward wouldn't be protected from the nimbus, etc. Likewise, if too many mages are easily able to think of Eddy as just short for Edward, the whole thing COULD be in danger. But as long as Eddy makes sure to uphold the symbolism of his name, it shouldn't be a problem.<br /> <br /> Of course, if he went plural, Eddies, it is probably different enough to make it work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T15:26:26-07:00","id":1496225,"title":"","content":"Physical approximation doesn't matter, symbolic one does. Their mundane name can be Edward and they behave one way. <br /> <br /> But when they become Eddy, they are a Moros embodying the role of Edward Elric. Their wear a red jacked with an Oroboros symbol, they have a metal gauntlet augmenting an arm (a multitool or weapon), they use alchemical symbolism, are more confident, have different body language and mannerisms. So symbolically the Tapestry sees them as two different people, so no problem.<br /> <br /> But if they behave similarly, dress similarly, have a similar name and so on, then the Shadow Name won't do its job of grounding their Nimbus to only affect their mage self. Mechanically, I would say this would happen if both are similar and the mage doesn't have a dot in Shadow Name. Mysteries, adversaries and other phenomena will be drawn to them in circumstances where its harder to practice discretion. <br /> <br /> If they choose a different Shadow Name and practice basic separation of their personas, this effect lessens to standard levels. If they purchase a dot in Shadow Name (whether its similar or not) by doing the work to establish the magical persona, then the merit's benefits make things easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T07:59:57-07:00","id":1496252,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar935_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"935\" data-vbnamecard=\"935\">Cleverest of Things</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> for the answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's make it a more accurate scenario:<ul><li>His full name is <b>James Edward Hall</b>.</li> <li>For most sleeper purposes (banks records, state and federal data), people refer to him as <b>James Hall</b>.</li> <li>Currently, he only lives to be a mage, no sleeper life at all. All his needs covered by magic, his social network is only mages and the occasional other (werewolf, vampire, changeling) that crosses paths.</li> <li><i>Former </i>coworkers at last job knew him as <b>Eddie</b>. All other previous jobs, university friends, schoolmates, childhood friends, etc, know him as <b>James</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> So, for this mage:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Will the name <b>Eddy </b>protect <b>Edward</b> even if it an homophone of his nickname <b>Eddie</b>? Mainly thinking of sympathetic magic here.</li> <li>Will the name <b>Eddy </b>protect his <b>former sleeper contacts</b>, even if it an homophone of his nickname <b>Eddie</b>? Thinking of resonances AND sympathetic magic here.</li> </ol><br /> Thanks,<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T08:48:54-07:00","id":1496254,"title":"","content":"I believe it will not, since James has no significant symbolism. He stopped or paused his Sleeper life to pursue his mage life, one transitioned into the other, which means his contacts will be under the effects of his Nimbus. <br /> <br /> In terms of Arcadian logic, actor E was playing role A, then he moved to role B. Arcadia needs to move the story of A forward, so it merges it with B, since E was playing the role before. Now E is playing B taking over the story of A, rather than switching between the roles of A and B.<br /> <br /> In addition, being a mage 24/7 is grating on one's Wisdom. Unless you have a very good reason (like suspecting an assassination plot against you), being constantly boosted to superhuman levels or having your daily necessities conveniently solved by magic will make you lose a reference point for normal. The supernatural is also actively dangerous, so being constantly exposed to insane spirits, Lovecraftian horrors, terrors from beyond the veil of death and much more will severely affect their overall wellness. So it wouldn't be surprising if someone in their Order sat them down for a talk, if not for concern then because they don't want to deal with a Rapt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-05-2022, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T10:35:27-07:00","id":1496259,"title":"","content":"I think the information on Shadow Names really conveys a lot of useful insight here.<br /> <br /> For a start, there's a clearly established standard for what a person's sympathetic name is given at the start of the description of the Space Arcanum; it's the name people (specifically people with Strong sympathetic links to you) called you by the first time you started forming sympathetic links to other people during infancy (said to be the time a child begins forming a sense of self). If he was called James (Hall) at the time, then that is the permanent name for sympathetic magic purposes, barring the intervention of magic. If he was called by a nickname from the outset, then <i>that</i> is the sympathetic name, even if his technical legal name is James. <br /> <br /> Sympathetic names are specific, so a modified form will not suffice if it's all the mage knows.<br /> <br /> I'd say that using a Shadow Name that is identical to your sympathetic name for the purposes of stopping sympathetic magic is basically useless, even if it's meant as a homonym. Like, if a mage knows your name is Eddy, they're not going to confuse themselves into thinking they're visualising the meaning in terms of air flow when they're casting a spell.<br /> <br /> On the other side, Shadow Name for the purposes of preventing your Nimbus from leaking along your sympathetic connections goes a bit deeper than just having a different moniker when encountering other mages. Even if you don't go deep enough for it to be represented by the Merit, the assumption is still that a mage adopts certain differences in persona that give the Shadow Name some substance. Some of this description of how the mage lives does sound like it gives it that backing, although frankly it also sounds like the mage is also detaching himself from most of what a Shadow Name would protect anyway.<br /> <br /> Of course, there's more to a Shadow Name than the functionally practical, there are deep rooted cultural reasons to why mages primarily use them among one another, and don't exactly treat them casually either.<br /> <br /> Hmm... I think somebody needs to <i>know</i> that something is your sympathetic name before they could use it in a spell, so a person who has been called Eddy their whole life could still present that in a context where mages wouldn't immediately peg it as a personal name and be safe. And I think the surname does also need to be known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T10:52:07-07:00","id":1496260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496254#post1496254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it will not, since James has no significant symbolism. He stopped or paused his Sleeper life to pursue his mage life, one transitioned into the other, which means his contacts will be under the effects of his Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but be aware that there are two questions above your post, one regarding sympathetic magic and another about resonances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496259#post1496259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the information on Shadow Names really conveys a lot of useful insight here.<br /> <br /> For a start, there's a clearly established standard for what a person's sympathetic name is given at the start of the description of the Space Arcanum; it's the name people (specifically people with Strong sympathetic links to you) called you by the first time you started forming sympathetic links to other people during infancy (said to be the time a child begins forming a sense of self). If he was called James (Hall) at the time, then that is the permanent name for sympathetic magic purposes, barring the intervention of magic. If he was called by a nickname from the outset, then <i>that</i> is the sympathetic name, even if his technical legal name is James.<br /> <br /> Sympathetic names are specific, so a modified form will not suffice if it's all the mage knows.<br /> <br /> I'd say that using a Shadow Name that is identical to your sympathetic name for the purposes of stopping sympathetic magic is basically useless, even if it's meant as a homonym. Like, if a mage knows your name is Eddy, they're not going to confuse themselves into thinking they're visualising the meaning in terms of air flow when they're casting a spell.<br /> <br /> On the other side, Shadow Name for the purposes of preventing your Nimbus from leaking along your sympathetic connections goes a bit deeper than just having a different moniker when encountering other mages. Even if you don't go deep enough for it to be represented by the Merit, the assumption is still that a mage adopts certain differences in persona that give the Shadow Name some substance. Some of this description of how the mage lives does sound like it gives it that backing, although frankly it also sounds like the mage is also detaching himself from most of what a Shadow Name would protect anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>James Hall</b> would be his sympathetic name in this case, but his Shadow Name is very close to one of his multiple personal names. So <i>for purposes of sympathetic magic</i> does Eddy suffice as protection? I think it does. <i>For purposes of Nimbus leaking (and sympathetic tracing)</i> does Eddy suffice as protection? I think it also works. But those are my opinions, I wanted some confirmation from more experienced gamers here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T13:54:40-07:00","id":1496275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496260#post1496260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>James Hall</b> would be his sympathetic name in this case, but his Shadow Name is very close to one of his multiple personal names. So <i>for purposes of sympathetic magic</i> does Eddy suffice as protection?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're talking about in terms of keeping the sympathetic name a secret, then any alias or nickname will suffice for that.<br /> <br /> Looking back at the Shadow Name Merit, I do see how that has a benefit of increasing the Withstand rating for sympathetic magic that is targeting the mage when in their Sleeper persona, so... On the one hand, it's not really a matter of how different the name is, but how much of a persona one creates and lives by it. If a person wants Eddy to provide extra protection, then live by that wind symbolism in a way that makes it clear that it's not just the shorthand nickname for Edward.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you've said this character has no mundane persona, so no, it wouldn't protect them more on that front. There's nothing <i>for</i> it to protect.<br /> <br /> Really, there are diminishing returns on the whole &quot;all mage all the time&quot; thing, if there's never a point when they get relief from the Nimbus.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-05T14:18:54-07:00","id":1496276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496275#post1496275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're talking about in terms of keeping the sympathetic name a secret, then any alias or nickname will suffice for that.<br /> <br /> Looking back at the Shadow Name Merit, I do see how that has a benefit of increasing the Withstand rating for sympathetic magic that is targeting the mage when in their Sleeper persona, so... On the one hand, it's not really a matter of how different the name is, but how much of a persona one creates and lives by it. If a person wants Eddy to provide extra protection, then live by that wind symbolism in a way that makes it clear that it's not just the shorthand nickname for Edward.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you've said this character has no mundane persona, so no, it wouldn't protect them more on that front. There's nothing <i>for</i> it to protect.<br /> <br /> Really, there are diminishing returns on the whole &quot;all mage all the time&quot; thing, if there's never a point when they get relief from the Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see, thanks.<br /> <br /> What about the exact same situation, but trying to keep some sleeper contacts: a girlfriend, a pet, a day job? Will the name (with all the other examples and conditions that I have stated already: same name as a nickname) provide protection to the Nimbus leaking effect?<br /> <br /> It could be that one of the sleepers hear someone refering to James as Eddy, and assume is a nickname. Best example would be a parent or a girlfriend, that would know the second name.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-06T14:57:34-08:00","id":1496332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496276#post1496276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the exact same situation, but trying to keep some sleeper contacts: a girlfriend, a pet, a day job? Will the name (with all the other examples and conditions that I have stated already: same name as a nickname) provide protection to the Nimbus leaking effect?<br /> <br /> It could be that one of the sleepers hear someone refering to James as Eddy, and assume is a nickname. Best example would be a parent or a girlfriend, that would know the second name.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description of the Shadow Name in relation to the Nimbus makes it come across as more than just a word. It's a matter of creating a separation of identity, of confining the use of the Art to when you present yourself as what you aspire your ideal Supernal self to be.<br /> <br /> I would say the Shadow Name won't be compromised just from people overhearing it, even if it isn't a homonym for a normal-sounding nickname. It's a question of what people have in mind when they address you by the name, whether you come off as different and, most importantly, whether you're casting spells on things that exist in your mundane life, or while you're in that identity.<br /> <br /> If a girlfriend calls you Eddy because they think of it as the short version of Edward, and you never cast spells on her or while on a date with her, I think one should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T10:39:34-08:00","id":1496511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1496192-shadow-name-too-close-to-your-real-name?p=1496332#post1496332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The description of the Shadow Name in relation to the Nimbus makes it come across as more than just a word. It's a matter of creating a separation of identity, of confining the use of the Art to when you present yourself as what you aspire your ideal Supernal self to be.<br /> <br /> I would say the Shadow Name won't be compromised just from people overhearing it, even if it isn't a homonym for a normal-sounding nickname. It's a question of what people have in mind when they address you by the name, whether you come off as different and, most importantly, whether you're casting spells on things that exist in your mundane life, or while you're in that identity.<br /> <br /> If a girlfriend calls you Eddy because they think of it as the short version of Edward, and you never cast spells on her or while on a date with her, I think one should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. It aligns with my ideas on the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T13:53:56-08:00","id":1496536,"title":"","content":"Reviewing the Storytelling chapter a bit, I would add the caveat that while there's probably nothing in the mechanisms of the Shadow Name that would be affected by such circumstances, culturally it might be something that puts other mages off a bit. I think they could generally be credited with managing to know the difference between Eddy as a nickname and Eddy as a term for wind current used as Shadow Name, but might still think the person using it like that is being a bit cavalier, even vulgar, with their choice of name. I'm imagining a scenario in which other mages in Eddy's presence when there's an uninitiated Sleeper talking to him wince a bit every time it's said, even if they know this Sleeper isn't actually using the Shadow Name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}